From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:52:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] atbm6031: drop a flush's frames when joined to nothing

After a firmware restart the AP is lost, and the scan that follows
recalculates idle under iflist_mtx, which flushes with a 7 s wait for
frames addressed to that AP; nothing can send them. wpa_supplicant's
authenticate waits on the same mutex: 7 s of every reconnect. Joined to
nothing, flush by dropping. A forced restart reconnects in 2.8 s, not
10.
---
 hal_apollo/sta.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hal_apollo/sta.c b/hal_apollo/sta.c
index b29bfb7..2d1dede 100644
--- a/hal_apollo/sta.c
+++ b/hal_apollo/sta.c
@@ -1383,6 +1383,9 @@ int __atbm_flush(struct atbm_common *hw_priv, bool drop, int if_id)
 		atbm_printk_err("%s:if_id[%d] is already reset\n",__func__,if_id);
 		return -1;
 	}
+	/* joined to nothing, its frames have no peer: waiting would sit out the timeout */
+	if (priv->join_status == ATBM_APOLLO_JOIN_STATUS_PASSIVE)
+		drop = true;
 	
 	for (;;) {
 		/* TODO: correct flush handling is required when dev_stop.
